{title: O Come, All Ye Faithful}
{lyricist: attributed to John F. Wade}
{translator: Frederick Oakeley}
{composer: John F. Wade}
{year: c. 1743}
{meta: translation-year 1841}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune ADESTE FIDELES}
{meta: variation The carol, sung to ADESTE FIDELES}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags Christmas}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [G]come, all ye [D]faithful, [G]joyful and [D]tri[G]umphant,
O [Em]come [D]ye, O [A]come ye to [D]Beth[A]le[D]hem;
[G]Come and be[C]hold Him, [G]born the [D]King of [G]angels:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
O [G]come, let us adore Him,
O come, let us a[D]dore Him,
O [G]come, let us [C]a[D]dore [Em]Him,
[C]Christ [D]the [G]Lord.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Sing, choirs of [D]angels, [G]sing in ex[D]ul[G]tation;
[Em]Sing, [D]all ye [A]citizens of [D]heaven [A]a[D]bove!
[G]Glory to [C]God, all [G]glory [D]in the [G]highest:
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Yea, Lord, we [D]greet Thee, [G]born this [D]happy [G]morning;
[Em]Je[D]sus, to [A]Thee be all [D]glory [A]giv[D]en;
[G]Word of the [C]Father, [G]now in [D]flesh ap[G]pearing:
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
